/* book: lead: The Carnot cycle is a closed loop of four reversible steps run between a hot reservoir at T₁ and a cold reservoir at T₂. It is the best engine possible between those two temperatures. Every real engine, from a Chennai backup generator to a coal power plant, is judged against it. Its efficiency depends only on T₁ and T₂, not on the gas, the size of the machine or the pressures used. */
/* book Figure 3.4.1: The worked example’s Carnot cycle on 1 kg of air between 900 K and 300 K. Left: the four states it passes through (the p-V shape is a sketch, because the volume grows thirtyfold). Right: the same cycle on T-S axes is a rectangle 0.199 kJ/K wide; its parts are W = 119.4 kJ and Q₂ = 59.7 kJ. */
